Third-party material
--------------------
The following original notices and obligations remain applicable in addition
to Apache-2.0 for local modifications:

* src/zupt_xxh.c and src/vv_xxh64.c adapt xxHash/XXH64 by Yann Collet:
  BSD-2-Clause; full notice in LICENSE-BSD-2-Clause.
  https://github.com/Cyan4973/xxHash

* src/zupt_mlkem.c adapts pq-crystals/kyber reference routines, including NTT,
  base multiplication and Montgomery representation. This distribution uses
  the upstream CC0-1.0 option; full text in LICENSE-CC0-1.0.
  https://github.com/pq-crystals/kyber

* src/zupt_x25519.c adapts curve25519-donna's field representation, packing,
  swap and inversion routines. Copyright 2008 Google Inc.; author Adam Langley.
  BSD-3-Clause; full notice in LICENSE-BSD-3-Clause.
  https://github.com/agl/curve25519-donna

* The x86 filter in src/vv_bcj.c adapts Igor Pavlov's public-domain LZMA SDK
  C/Bra86.c state machine. The AArch64 filter is separate first-party code.
  https://www.7-zip.org/sdk.html

* src/zupt_sha256_shani.c adapts Jeffrey Walton's public-domain SHA-Intrinsics
  sha256-x86.c, which credits Intel and Sean Gulley's miTLS material. Reference:
  https://github.com/noloader/SHA-Intrinsics/blob/d03795497f3e4576083fc2cd8fe0b924f24d0bb2/sha256-x86.c

The original adaptation revisions for xxHash, Kyber, curve25519-donna and LZMA
were not retained; no unverified revision is asserted here.

The textual Jasmin/assembly sources retain their per-file provenance. The
external Jasmin compiler is not bundled. A matching .jazz description does
not by itself establish a formal proof of the hand-written assembly.

The optional Bend proofs cover only the definitions and assumptions in
formal/aggregation.bend and LAWS.bend. They do not prove the C implementation,
cryptography, filesystem behavior, or operating system.

